;; repr/rust's read level's classes for bin/reap (the REAP row of Rust; test/reap/cells.edn's :rust :read): every unit of the tree
;; and interface levels' known files (test/rust/roundtrip-*-known.edn, "LEVEL: REASON") falls into one, the first whose :match finds
;; its "RESULT REASON"; goi's format (test/goi/divergences.edn). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :parser-rejects
  :title "a file rustc's parser rejects alone"
  :kind :design
  :why "a module whose text is one string literal (erased-serde's src/features_check/error.rs, which its mod.rs declares when no feature is chosen): rustc's own parser rejects the file alone (rust-lisp D20), so there are no trees to compare; the build of the crate fails with that message by design"
  :decided "RR4; doc/rust/RUST-NOTES.md, \"RR4\""
  :match [#"rustc's parser rejects the file alone"]}
 {:id :converter-depth
  :title "the converter's evaluated call depth"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the converter, evaluated by the tools' host, nests more than its 10,000 evaluated calls (Compiler's MAX_DEPTH, doc/go/J2G-SPEC.md section 10.5: Go's stack overflow is fatal) on three UI-suite files rustc's own stack tests (a type of 964 nested generic applications, an if with 5,204 else-ifs, the Peano queue): compiled, the converter has Go's goroutine stack"
  :decided "RR5; doc/rust/RUST-NOTES.md, \"RR5\""
  :match [#"nests more than its 10,000 evaluated calls"]}
 {:id :token-spacing
  :title "token spacing (N3)"
  :kind :design
  :why "rustdoc writes an attribute the derived impls copy with its tokens' spacing (nom's #[allow(deprecated,missing_docs)]), which mode :lines prints its own: the interface level compares rustdoc's JSON, spacing is the layout's (SPEC N3)"
  :decided "RR4; SPEC section 11.5"
  :match [#"token spacing \(N3\)"]}
]
